# plan.env: the placement plan results/margin.md declares, read by plan.sh (build.sh, verify.sh,
# run.sh) and report.mjs. Written before any binary was built or measured. pads.mjs writes and
# checks the pad lists: the first 30 of each are kit 1965's.
#   K              placements per comparison
#   R              recorded pairs per placement, after one unrecorded pair
#   PADS_P         the pad of side A's placement i (bytes): base's A side in the A/A comparisons, and
#                  in the change comparisons the pad of both base and head (base pad p_i against
#                  head pad p_i)
#   PADS_Q         the pad of base's B side in the A/A comparisons (base pad p_i against base pad q_i)
#   WIN_WORKLOAD   the one workload a CPU-cost reduction is declared for
#   WIN_REDUCTION  its smallest worthwhile reduction, a share of user plus kernel cycles a request
# A pad of n bytes is one never-called function of n bytes linked first in .text (build.sh), so
# every function after it moves by n and keeps its order.
K=60
R=8
PADS_P="320 15120 25824 40624 10304 21008 35808 5552 20288 30992 736 15536 26176 36880 10720 21424 36160 5904 16608 31408 1088 15888 26592 37296 11072 21776 36576 6320 16960 31760 1504 16304 26944 37648 11488 22192 32832 6672 17376 32176 1856 12560 27360 38064 11840 22544 33248 7088 17728 32528 2272 12976 27712 38416 12256 22960 33600 7440 18144 28848"
PADS_Q="22848 12160 38336 27648 12880 2192 32464 17680 7008 33184 22496 11808 38000 27312 12528 1840 32064 17280 6592 32768 22096 11408 37584 26896 16224 1440 31712 16928 6256 36528 21808 11120 37248 26560 15872 5184 31376 16592 10000 36176 21408 14816 36896 26208 19632 752 31024 20336 5504 35776 20992 14400 40592 25808 19216 336 30624 19936 5152 35424"
WIN_WORKLOAD=api
WIN_REDUCTION=0.01
